The build pipeline under native/ (PINS, build.sh, docker-build.sh, patches/,
and the Kotlin runtime layer in app/src/main/java/com/olyphototagger/app/exiftool/
that extracts and invokes the resulting binaries) is adapted from:

    exiftoolwrapper-android
    https://github.com/bestvibes/exiftoolwrapper-android
    Copyright (c) 2019 Vaibhav Aggarwal

used under the MIT License below. Changes made here: package name
(me.bestvibes.exiftoolwrapper -> com.olyphototagger.app), pinned versions
(ExifTool 13.57 -> 13.59, NDK r26d -> r27d — see native/PINS for why), and
scope — this app invokes a single fixed GPS-write command it constructs
itself, not a general user-facing exiftool command builder, so the slot-based
CommandParser/CommandModel/Presets/UI layer from the original project was not
carried over.

